# Which node and wallet images this deploy runs (#247).
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. The z3-stack compose file is a separate upstream project
# checked out beside ours, and its image lines carry defaults. With no override we
# inherited somebody else's default, so the version of the node our funds depend on
# was not a PR in this repo, had no review gate, and `docker inspect` on the box was
# the only way to find out what we ran. The July 28 advisory described old Zebra
# nodes halting silently at an activation height; we were fine, and we only knew
# that because a person checked by hand.
#
# HOW IT IS USED. z3-stack reads `.env` beside its compose file, so this is copied
# there by install-ops.sh. Changing a version here is therefore a reviewable PR,
# and audit-drift.sh compares these against what is actually running so a box that
# stops matching is reported rather than discovered.
#
# CHANGING A VERSION IS NOT ENOUGH ON ITS OWN. The stack has to be pulled and
# restarted for a new pin to take effect, so a drift line after an edit here is
# expected until the redeploy happens. See REDEPLOY.md.

# Zebra, the consensus node. Version state format matters for snapshot import:
# v6.0.0, v6.2.0 and the fork all declare state format 28.0.0 (see SNAPSHOTS.md),
# so those are interchangeable for a restore. Do not assume that holds across a
# major without checking zebra-state/src/constants.rs.
Z3_ZEBRA_IMAGE=zfnd/zebra:6.2.0

# The wallet. This is a THIRD-PARTY build (zodlinc), not a Zcash Foundation or ECC
# one, which is #184's finding and the reason it is written down here rather than
# left implicit. Hard gate: no third-party wallet build against mainnet funds.
#
# Left unset deliberately. The tag we run is only knowable from the box, and
# guessing it would put a wrong number under review, which is worse than an
# admitted gap. Fill it from:
#   docker inspect -f '{{.Config.Image}}' "$(docker ps --filter name=zallet --format '{{.Names}}' | head -n1)"
# audit-drift.sh reports an unpinned component as NOT VERIFIED rather than passing it.
#Z3_ZALLET_IMAGE=

# Zaino, the light-client indexer. Nothing to pin by default: the overlay does not
# start a standalone indexer and points at a public Zaino for read-side lookups
# (see README.md). Set this only if you self-host it with --profile indexer.
#Z3_ZAINO_IMAGE=
